29.03.2006, 22:34 Jorge Llambías wrote:

> Sometimes when I click on "Review Translations" I get the message
> "Sorry, currently there are no translations you can review." when there
> are in fact translations I have not reviewed yet. Is there a cap on the
> number of reviews one can make? (If so, why?) If I go to the translations
> through another way (the "current rating list" or the "posts" buttons)
> I will be allowed to review them, but then I know who the translation
> is from, and I think it's better to review without knowing that. So, there
> seems to be a bug there one way or the other.

The system looks for translations that:
- haven't been reviewed by you earlier;
- haven't been skipped by you earlier;
- are not translations of void posts;
- are not abandoned;
- fit into your difficulty span;
- were not created by a banned user.

If you are sure a particular translation doesn't fall under any of
these restrictions, and still it doesn't appear in "Review
Translations", it's definitely a bug. Unfortunately, the jsk database
is on Robin's server and it's impossible for me to debug. :(


